WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.458
A package gives a type a qualified address. Package school dot people, class Student, means school dot people dot Student. Moving the source file alone does not change that identity. The declaration does.

00:00:14.458 --> 00:00:30.417
An import lets one source file use Student as a short name. It does not install the class, copy its source, or grant access to a hidden constructor. A wildcard imports types directly in one package, not its subpackages.

00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:47.042
Below the source root, folders mirror the package. The compiler reads dot java files and writes dot class files. The d option chooses the output root. Sourcepath chooses where source dependencies can be found. They have different jobs.

00:00:47.042 --> 00:01:04.917
To run school dot app dot Main, point the classpath at classes, the root above school. Java appends the package path and class filename. Pointing at classes slash school repeats school in the lookup path. Run the qualified name without the dot class extension.

00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:24.333
Diagnose the layer before changing code. Cannot find symbol suggests a name or lookup problem. Not public is an access problem. Main method not found means the selected class was found, but the required entry point is missing. More imports cannot repair all three.
